category: Audio
build-depends: cygport 
sdesc: "Convert CD images from .bin/.cue to .iso/.cdr"
ldesc: "binchunker converts a CD image in a '.bin / .cue' format (sometimes
'.raw / .cue') to a set of .iso and .cdr tracks. The bin/cue format is used by
some popular non-Unix cd-writing software, but is not supported on most other CD
burning programs. A lot of CD/VCD images distributed on the Internet are in
BIN/CUE format, I've been told."
skip:

homepage: http://he.fi/bchunk/
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
